eatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia to reduce morbidity and mortality.", "HERRAMIENTAS VALIDADAS:Validated tools that assist in the early detection of oropharyngeal dysphagia, applicable to all patients at risk.", "SÍNTOMAS MANIFIESTOS:Manifest symptoms of dysphagia include difficulty swallowing, nasal regurgitation, and coughing during food intake.", "SÍNTOMAS SILENTES:Silent symptoms of dysphagia may include changes in eating habits and respiratory infections.", "CALIDAD DE VIDA:\"Calidad de vida\" refers to the general well-being and life satisfaction of individuals and societies, encompassing various factors that can influence this state. It is particularly relevant in the context of health conditions and interventions, such as in patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC), chronic gastrointestinal symptoms, and neurological diseases. The quality of life can be negatively affected by these health issues, but it can also be improved through adequate nutritional treatment and medical care.\n\nIn healthcare, quality of life is often measured through cost-utility analyses and questionnaires, which assess how various factors, including nutrition and underlying health conditions, impact an individual's overall well-being. For instance, patients suffering from dysphagia experience significant challenges that affect their social and emotional well-being, but early intervention and treatment can lead to improvements in their quality of life.\n\nMoreover, the impact of cancer and its treatment on quality of life underscores the importance of nutritional support, as it can significantly enhance the overall well-being of patients. Thus, \"calidad de vida\" encompasses a holistic view of health, emphasizing the interplay between medical treatments, caregiving responsibilities, and the nutritional status of individuals, ultimately highlighting the importance of tailored interventions to improve life satisfaction and well-being.", "TRASTORNOS DE LA DEGLUCIÓN:", "DR. P. CLAVÉ CIVIT:Dr. P. Clavé Civit is a medical professional who designed the clinical exploration method for assessing swallowing disorders, known as MECV-V or V-VST.", "MÉTODO DE EXPLORACIÓN CLÍNICA VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:The Método de Exploración Clínica Volumen-Viscosidad (MECV-V) is a non-invasive clinical assessment method specifically designed to evaluate dysphagia, which is a condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This method involves administering food at varying volumes and viscosities to assess the safety and efficacy of swallowing. By utilizing different bolus characteristics, the MECV-V aims to provide a comprehensive evaluation of an individual's swallowing capabilities, ensuring a thorough understanding of their condition.", "ACIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR AGUDO:Acute cerebrovascular accident (ACVA) refers to a medical emergency that can lead to swallowing difficulties, necessitating specific screening methods for dysphagia.", "BOLUS:BOLUS refers to a mass of substance, typically food or liquid, that is swallowed. It plays a crucial role in the assessment of swallowing disorders, as it is the material that is evaluated during such assessments. Specifically, the bolus is the mass of food that is prepared in the oral cavity for swallowing, making it an essential component in understanding and diagnosing swallowing difficulties.", "PULSOXÍMETRO:A pulse oximeter is a medical device used to monitor the oxygen saturation of a patient's blood, often used during swallowing assessments to detect silent aspirations.", "MOVILIDAD DE LA MANDÍBULA:Jaw mobility involves the movement of the jaw in various directions, which is crucial for effective chewing and swallowing.", "SENSIBILIDAD OROFARÍNGEA:Oropharyngeal sensitivity refers to the ability to feel sensations in the oral and pharyngeal areas, which is important for triggering the swallowing reflex."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "prese